('127.685.d.5.E',4,'A global issue that affects web design is that visitors:','["never use phones", "all use one language", "never leave", "come from different countries with different laws"]'::jsonb,3,'Global audiences face varying rules.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.F',3,'A safe online shared workspace should limit access to:','["authorized team members", "everyone in the world", "anyone who asks", "strangers"]'::jsonb,0,'Access control protects shared work.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.F',4,'Setting different permissions for viewers and editors on a shared project helps:','["slow it", "protect the work from unwanted changes", "hide it", "delete it"]'::jsonb,1,'Roles control what users can do.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.G',3,'Website marketing is unethical when it:','["shows real photos", "tells the truth", "makes false claims about a product", "lists accurate prices"]'::jsonb,2,'Honesty is required.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.G',4,'Collecting email addresses for marketing without asking permission is:','["required", "always allowed", "a good practice", "not appropriate and may be illegal"]'::jsonb,3,'Consent is needed for marketing.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.H',3,'Before putting a video clip from another creator on your website, you should:','["get permission or confirm a license", "edit the credit", "assume it''s free", "claim it"]'::jsonb,0,'Using video requires rights.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.H',4,'Adding background music to a business site is safe if the music is:','["ripped from a disc", "royalty-free or properly licensed", "downloaded illegally", "copied from radio"]'::jsonb,1,'Licensed music avoids infringement.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.I',3,'One way the Web has changed society is by making it easier to:','["stop learning", "slow news", "share information quickly around the world", "limit communication"]'::jsonb,2,'The Web speeds sharing.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.I',4,'Researchers studying the Web''s impact might use:','["guesses only", "rumors", "fiction", "surveys, interviews and data analysis"]'::jsonb,3,'Research uses evidence.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.J',3,'Building a free website for a local nonprofit is an example of:','["community involvement", "a waste of time", "a crime", "a vacation"]'::jsonb,0,'Service benefits the community.','original'),
('127.685.d.5.J',4,'A student who helps older adults learn to use email is:','["breaking rules", "participating in a meaningful community activity", "avoiding work", "wasting time"]'::jsonb,1,'Helping others builds community.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.A',3,'A digital camera, a printer and a video camera are all examples of:','["search engines", "domain names", "computer peripherals", "web hosts"]'::jsonb,2,'Peripherals connect to a computer.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.A',4,'A web designer who needs to put printed artwork on a website would use a:','["firewall", "modem", "router", "scanner"]'::jsonb,3,'Scanners digitize artwork.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.B',3,'The part of a computer that stores programs and files long term is the:','["storage drive", "speaker", "cable", "fan"]'::jsonb,0,'Drives provide permanent storage.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.B',4,'The motherboard''s role in a computer is to:','["print documents", "connect and let the major parts communicate", "store all files", "display images"]'::jsonb,1,'It links components.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.C',3,'Web servers are needed because they:','["cool rooms", "play music", "hold websites and deliver them on request", "print files"]'::jsonb,2,'Servers respond to browser requests.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.C',4,'A file server on a company network is used to:','["play games", "print posters", "edit video", "store and share files among users"]'::jsonb,3,'File servers centralize storage.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.D',3,'Running your own web server at home can mean you must handle:','["hardware, security and constant uptime yourself", "no maintenance", "nothing", "no electricity"]'::jsonb,0,'Self-hosting requires effort.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.D',4,'Using a hosting provider instead of a personal server often provides:','["more downtime", "professional support and reliable connections", "less security", "no backups"]'::jsonb,1,'Providers offer managed service.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.E',3,'Which device is part of the processing stage of a computer?','["the keyboard", "the printer", "the CPU", "the monitor"]'::jsonb,2,'The CPU processes data.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.E',4,'A flash drive that saves files is an example of:','["a monitor", "an input device", "a processor", "secondary storage"]'::jsonb,3,'Secondary storage keeps data.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.F',3,'A universally accessible document can be used by people:','["with and without disabilities", "only experts", "only students", "only designers"]'::jsonb,0,'Universal design includes everyone.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.F',4,'Adding captions to a video makes it accessible to viewers who are:','["far away", "deaf or hard of hearing", "in a hurry", "blind only"]'::jsonb,1,'Captions convey audio.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.G',3,'A website for a worldwide audience should consider the audience''s:','["shoe size", "hair color", "connection speeds", "favorite food"]'::jsonb,2,'Bandwidth varies globally.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.G',4,'Higher-capacity hosting plans usually cost more, so a site owner must balance bandwidth needs against:','["logo", "name", "color", "budget"]'::jsonb,3,'Cost limits capacity choices.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.H',3,'Storing all images for a site in one folder named ''images'' is part of:','["a folder hierarchy", "a virus", "a hack", "an error"]'::jsonb,0,'Folders organize assets.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.H',4,'If a page''s image folder is moved without updating the code, the images will show as:','["sharper", "broken", "faster", "bigger"]'::jsonb,1,'Paths must match the structure.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.I',3,'Naming files without spaces or special characters helps avoid:','["faster typing", "good design", "problems in web addresses", "extra color"]'::jsonb,2,'Plain names work reliably.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.I',4,'The file name ''my-photo-1.jpg'' follows the guideline of:','["emoji", "uppercase only", "spaces and symbols", "lowercase letters and hyphens"]'::jsonb,3,'It is clean and safe for the web.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.J',3,'White space on a web page helps by:','["giving content room so it is easier to read", "hiding content", "adding clutter", "deleting text"]'::jsonb,0,'Space improves clarity.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.J',4,'Contrast, alignment and repetition are all examples of:','["HTML tags", "basic design principles", "server brands", "file types"]'::jsonb,1,'They guide layout decisions.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.K',3,'The domain extension .edu is usually used by:','["government agencies", "military units", "educational institutions", "nonprofits only"]'::jsonb,2,'.edu is for education.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.K',4,'Which pair correctly matches a domain extension with its usual meaning?','["mil and commercial", "com and military", "org and education", "gov and government agency"]'::jsonb,3,'.gov is for government.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.L',3,'HTML is used to:','["structure the content of a web page", "style printers", "edit audio", "cool servers"]'::jsonb,0,'HTML defines page structure.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.L',4,'Cascading style sheets (CSS) are used mainly to:','["send email", "control the look of web pages", "host videos", "store passwords"]'::jsonb,1,'CSS handles presentation.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.M',3,'FTP client software is used to:','["print pages", "scan images", "upload site files to a web server", "play audio"]'::jsonb,2,'FTP clients transfer files.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.M',4,'Before connecting with an FTP client, a user usually needs the server address and:','["a poster", "a printer", "a scanner", "a username and password"]'::jsonb,3,'Credentials authenticate the user.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.N',3,'A Java applet is a small program that:','["runs inside a web page", "burns discs", "prints pages", "edits photos"]'::jsonb,0,'Applets embed in pages.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.N',4,'Many modern browsers have stopped supporting Java applets mainly because of:','["slow printers", "security concerns and newer technologies", "too many colors", "too many fonts"]'::jsonb,1,'Applets were replaced by safer options.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.O',3,'A network in which every device connects to a central switch has a:','["bus topology", "mesh topology", "star topology", "ring topology"]'::jsonb,2,'Star uses a central device.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.O',4,'A topology that describes how data actually flows, rather than how cables are laid out, is the:','["paper topology", "physical topology", "building topology", "logical topology"]'::jsonb,3,'Logical shows data paths.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.P',3,'A web-based animation can be created to:','["make a page more engaging", "hide content", "remove links", "slow all pages"]'::jsonb,0,'Animation adds interest.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.P',4,'Too many large animations on one page can:','["fix errors", "make it load slowly", "speed it up", "reduce file size"]'::jsonb,1,'Heavy animation hurts performance.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.Q',3,'Compressing a video before putting it on a website makes the file:','["blank", "corrupted", "smaller", "larger"]'::jsonb,2,'Compression reduces size.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.Q',4,'After editing video for the web, a creator exports it in a format such as:','["CSV", "TXT", "DOC", "MP4"]'::jsonb,3,'MP4 plays in browsers.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.R',3,'A web page that begins with https uses a:','["secure connection to the server", "slower connection only", "unknown connection", "broken connection"]'::jsonb,0,'HTTPS encrypts traffic.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.R',4,'Encrypting data sent from a web form protects visitors'' information from:','["being loaded", "being read by outsiders", "being seen by the owner", "being typed"]'::jsonb,1,'Encryption stops eavesdropping.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.S',3,'A hyperlink on a web page allows the user to:','["print the page", "close the browser", "jump to another page or resource", "turn off the computer"]'::jsonb,2,'Links connect pages.','original'),
('127.685.d.6.S',4,'For accessibility, link text should be:','["a random symbol", "just the word ''click''", "blank", "descriptive of where the link goes"]'::jsonb,3,'Descriptive links help all users.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
